## Dimension 3: Security
### Applicable Guardrails
- **SEC-001:** TLS encryption in transit — all webhook and email traffic over HTTPS
- **WSEC-006a:** encodeURIComponent() for any user-supplied values embedded in URLs
- **WSEC-013:** @emisgroup/acp-security-headers in dependencies
### Security Requirements
- **Authentication:** No authentication required to submit escalation (widget is public-facing)
- **Authorisation:** N/A for end user; Teams webhook URL must be stored as environment secret, not hardcoded
- **Encryption in Transit:** TLS 1.2+ for webhook POST and confirmation email dispatch
- **Encryption at Rest:** Email addresses stored only transiently for dispatch; no long-term storage unless retention policy confirmed
- **Teams Webhook URL:** Must be stored as environment variable / secret — never committed to source code
### Data Subject Rights
- **Article 15 (Access):** Partner developer may request access to their escalation data
- **Article 17 (Erasure):** Email and chat history must be erasable on request
- **Article 20 (Portability):** Escalation data exportable on request
- Note: Retention policy and erasure mechanism to be confirmed with IG owner before go-live
