## ✨ Evaluation Function Specification
**PURPOSE:** Define DETERMINISTIC pass/fail criteria for coding agents to verify implementation.
---
### CHECK 1: Email Format Validation (RFC 5322)
**Trigger:** User submits email address in escalation form
**Test Scenario 1: Invalid email rejected**
- **Input:** `"notanemail"` (no @ symbol)
- **Expected Response:** Inline validation error displayed
- **Expected Message:** "Please enter a valid email address"
- **Validation:** No webhook fired, no confirmation email sent
**Test Scenario 2: Another invalid format rejected**
- **Input:** `"user@"` (missing domain)
- **Expected Response:** Inline validation error displayed
- **Expected Message:** "Please enter a valid email address"
**Test Scenario 3: Valid email accepted**
- **Input:** `"developer@partner.com"`
- **Expected Response:** Submission proceeds, confirmation shown
- **Pass Criteria:** Invalid emails blocked with error message; valid emails proceed to dispatch
**Applicable Guardrail:** IG-001 (Data Minimisation — only valid data collected)
**Pass Criteria:** Invalid email formats REJECTED with user-friendly message; valid formats ACCEPTED
---
### CHECK 2: Teams Webhook Payload Completeness
**Trigger:** Valid escalation submitted
**Test Scenario: Webhook payload contains all required fields**
- **Setup:** Submit valid escalation after bot fails to answer
- **Validation 1:** Webhook POST fired to configured Teams URL
- **Validation 2:** Payload contains `email` field
- **Validation 3:** Payload contains `chat_history` (array of messages)
- **Validation 4:** Payload contains `triggering_question` (string)
- **Validation 5:** Payload contains `page_url` (string, valid URL)
- **Validation 6:** Payload contains `timestamp` (ISO 8601 format)
- **Forbidden in payload:** Full email address in plain text in logs
**Applicable Guardrail:** SEC-001 (TLS in transit), IG-001 (Data Minimisation)
**Pass Criteria:** All 6 fields present in webhook payload; dispatched within 5s of submission
---
### CHECK 3: Confirmation Email Sent to Partner
**Trigger:** Valid escalation submitted
**Test Scenario: Confirmation email dispatched**
- **Setup:** Submit valid escalation with `developer@partner.com`
- **Validation 1:** Email dispatched to `developer@partner.com`
- **Validation 2:** Email contains polite confirmation message
- **Validation 3:** Email dispatched within 5s of submission
- **Anti-pattern:** Email sent before webhook confirmation (webhook must fire first)
**Applicable Guardrail:** SEC-001 (TLS in transit)
**Pass Criteria:** Confirmation email sent to provided address within 5s; polite message included
---
### CHECK 4: In-Widget Confirmation Message
**Trigger:** Successful escalation submission
**Test Scenario: User sees confirmation in widget**
- **Input:** Valid email submitted
- **Expected UI State:** Escalation form replaced with confirmation message
- **Expected Message:** "Thanks for reaching out — we've received your question and will be in touch soon."
- **Validation:** Form inputs no longer visible after submission (prevent double-submit)
**Applicable Guardrail:** DS-001 (@emisgroup/ui-* components used for confirmation state)
**Pass Criteria:** Confirmation message displayed; form hidden; double-submit prevented
---
### CHECK 5: Idempotency — No Double Escalation
**Trigger:** User clicks submit twice (double-click or network delay)
**Test Scenario: Second submission within same session**
- **Action:** Submit escalation, then submit again immediately
- **Expected:** Only ONE webhook fired, ONE confirmation email sent
- **Expected UI:** Submit button disabled after first successful submission
- **Anti-pattern:** Two identical Teams notifications for same conversation
**Applicable Guardrail:** SEC-001
**Pass Criteria:** Exactly one webhook and one email per escalation event; submit button disabled post-submission
---
### CHECK 6: Webhook URL Stored as Secret
**Trigger:** Code review / deployment check
**Test Scenario: Webhook URL not hardcoded**
- **Validation 1:** No Teams webhook URL present in source code or committed config files
- **Validation 2:** Webhook URL loaded from environment variable (e.g. `TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL`)
- **Validation 3:** Application fails to start with meaningful error if `TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL` not set
**Applicable Guardrail:** SEC-001, WSEC-013
**Pass Criteria:** Webhook URL ONLY in environment config; never in source code
---
### CHECK A: DS-001 — @emisgroup Components Only
**Trigger:** Any UI component in escalation flow rendered
**Test Scenario: No native HTML interactive elements**
- **Validation:** No `<input>`, `<button>`, `<form>`, `<textarea>` in escalation component source
- **Expected:** `@emisgroup/ui-*` equivalents used throughout
- **Pass Criteria:** Zero native interactive HTML elements in component tree
---
### CHECK B: A11Y-004a — Input Accessibility
**Trigger:** Email input field rendered
**Test Scenario: Input has accessible label**
- **Validation 1:** Email input has `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, or associated `htmlFor`
- **Validation 2:** Error message linked to input via `aria-describedby`
- **Pass Criteria:** All inputs labelled; error messages programmatically associated
---
### CHECK C: A11Y-010 — jest-axe
**Trigger:** Component test file executed
**Test Scenario: No accessibility violations**
- **Validation:** `toHaveNoViolations()` passes for escalation form component
- **Pass Criteria:** Zero axe violations reported
---
### CHECK D: WCS-007a / WCS-007b — i18n and British English
**Trigger:** Any user-facing string rendered
**Test Scenario: All strings use t() and British English**
- **Validation 1:** No hardcoded English strings in JSX
- **Validation 2:** All strings in `src/locales/en-GB/translation.json`
- **Validation 3:** British English spellings used (e.g. "colour", "centre")
- **Pass Criteria:** Zero hardcoded strings; all translations in en-GB file
